IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bnra-types`

-- Business Names Registration Act 2014, Part 1 (ss 1 to 4).
-- Source: source/BNRA2014.txt lines 80 to 379.
--
-- Section 1 (short title) is inert.  Section 2(1) is a list of definitions; each
-- one the Act relies on is a rule here.  Definitions that only point elsewhere
-- ("ACRA administered Act", "Authority", "company", "foreign company", "inspector",
-- "register", "registered", "Registrar" and the terms defined by reference to other
-- sections) are facts in bnra-types.l4 or are decided in the section they name.
-- Section 2(1) opens with a definition deleted by Act 21 of 2024.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `2(1) "business"`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(1) 'business'"
GIVEN b IS A `Business Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a business` IF
        (   b's `the activity is a form of trade, commerce or profession`
         OR b's `the activity is any other activity`)
    AND b's `the activity is carried on for the purposes of gain`
    AND NOT b's `the activity is an office, employment or occupation`

§§ `2(1) "individual", "corporation", "firm"`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(1) 'individual' (a) and (b)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Individual Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an individual` IF
        i's `the person is a natural person`
     OR (    (   i's `the person is an administrator, an executor, a liquidator, a trustee, a nominee or a guardian of an individual`
              OR i's `the person is a donee or deputy appointed under the Mental Capacity Act 2008 in respect of an individual`)
         AND i's `the person has direct control or management of the business carried on by the individual`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(1) 'corporation' (a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN c IS A `Corporation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a corporation` IF
        c's `the body is a body corporate formed, incorporated or existing in Singapore or outside Singapore`
     OR c's `the body is a company`
     OR c's `the body is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
     OR c's `the body is a foreign company`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(1) 'firm' (a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN f IS A `Firm Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a firm` IF
        f's `the body is unincorporated`
    AND f's `the members have entered into partnership with one another with a view to carrying on business for profit`
    AND (   f's `the number of members who are individuals` AT LEAST 2
         OR (    f's `the number of members who are individuals` AT LEAST 1
             AND f's `the number of members who are corporations` AT LEAST 1)
         OR f's `the number of members who are corporations` AT LEAST 2)

§§ `2(1) "contact address", "full name"`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(1) 'contact address' (a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN a IS A `Contact Address Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the address is a contact address` IF
        a's `the address is a physical address at which the individual can be physically found or contacted by post`
    AND NOT a's `the address is a post office box number`
    AND a's `the address is located in the same jurisdiction as the individual's residential address`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(1) 'full name' (a) and (b)"
GIVEN n IS A `Full Name Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the individual's full name` MEANS
    IF n's `the individual is registered under the National Registration Act 1965`
    THEN n's `the name as it appears in the latest identity card issued to the individual`
    ELSE n's `the name as it appears in the latest passport issued to the individual or such other similar evidence of identification as is available`

§§ `2(2) and (3). Carrying on business in Singapore`

-- 2(2): a person who has a place of business in Singapore is treated as carrying on
-- business there.  2(3): despite that, a foreign company is not so treated "for the
-- reason only" that in Singapore it does one of (a) to (l).  So a foreign company whose
-- only reason is one or more of those activities is not treated as carrying on business,
-- and one with any other reason is.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(3)(a) to (l)"
GIVEN p IS A `Business Presence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign company does any of the activities in section 2(3)(a) to (l)` IF
        p's `in Singapore it is or becomes a party to an action, suit or proceeding, or effects a settlement`
     OR p's `in Singapore it holds meetings of its directors or shareholders or carries on other activities concerning its internal affairs`
     OR p's `in Singapore it maintains a bank account`
     OR p's `in Singapore it effects a sale through an independent contractor`
     OR p's `in Singapore it solicits or procures an order that becomes a binding contract only if accepted outside Singapore`
     OR p's `in Singapore it creates evidence of a debt or creates a charge on property`
     OR p's `in Singapore it secures or collects its debts or enforces its rights in regard to securities for them`
     OR p's `in Singapore it conducts an isolated transaction completed within 31 days that is not one of a number of similar transactions repeated from time to time`
     OR p's `in Singapore it invests any of its funds or holds any property`
     OR p's `in Singapore it establishes a share transfer or share registration office`
     OR p's `in Singapore it effects a transaction through its related corporation licensed or approved by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under an arrangement that Authority approved`
     OR p's `in Singapore it carries on another activity that has been prescribed`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 2(2) and (3)"
GIVEN p IS A `Business Presence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is treated as carrying on business in Singapore` IF
        p's `the person otherwise carries on business in Singapore`
     OR (    p's `the person has a place of business in Singapore`
         AND NOT (    p's `the person is a foreign company`
                  AND `the foreign company does any of the activities in section 2(3)(a) to (l)` p
                  AND NOT p's `it does something else in Singapore that is a reason for treating it as carrying on business`))

-- 2(4) defines "related corporation" by the Companies Act; 2(5) leaves the manner and
-- form of lodging to the Registrar; 2(6) extends "the Minister" in ss 8(7), 12(4), 16(5)
-- and 17(9), (10) to an authorised Minister of State.  None adds a condition: inert.

§§ `3. Administration of Act and appointment of Registrar of Business Names, etc.`

-- 3(1) to (5) vest the administration of the Act in the Authority, give the Minister the
-- power to appoint the Registrar and Deputy and Assistant Registrars, state the
-- Registrar's duties (keeping the register, collecting fees), let the Authority give
-- directions, and let the Registrar delegate everything but delegation.  They are
-- allocations of office and power that no fact of a case can satisfy or fail: inert.

§§ `4. Persons not required to be registered under Act`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 4(1)(c) and (2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the profession exemption in section 4(1)(c) applies` IF
        e's `an individual or a firm of 2 or more individuals carrying on business consisting solely of the exercise of a profession that under a written law can be exercised only by those who possess certain qualifications and whose names are registered or otherwise recorded as that law prescribes`
    AND NOT e's `regulations prescribe that the exemption for such a profession does not apply to the individual or firm`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 4(1)(o)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the limited partnership exemption in section 4(1)(o) applies` IF
        e's `a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
    AND NOT e's `section 42(3) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 removes the exemption for the limited partnership`

-- 4(1)(e) to (o): the bodies that may not choose to be registered (s 4(3)).

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 4(1)(e) to (o) and (ja)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is within section 4(1)(e) to (o)` IF
        e's `a statutory authority or other body established by or under a public Act for a public purpose`
     OR e's `an institution, authority, person or fund specified in the First Schedule to the Income Tax Act 1947`
     OR e's `a society registered under the Societies Act 1966`
     OR e's `a society registered under the Co-operative Societies Act 1979`
     OR e's `a mutual benefit organisation registered under the Mutual Benefit Organisations Act 1960`
     OR e's `a trade union registered under the Trade Unions Act 1940`
     OR e's `a platform work association registered under the Platform Workers Act 2024`
     OR e's `the Public Trustee or the Official Assignee of the property of a bankrupt`
     OR e's `a foreign company registered under the Companies Act 1967 that carries on business under its registered name`
     OR e's `a company carrying on business under its corporate name`
     OR e's `a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 carrying on business under its registered name`
     OR `the limited partnership exemption in section 4(1)(o) applies` e

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 4(1)(a) to (q)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is not required to be registered under section 4(1)` IF
        e's `an individual proprietor carrying on business under only the individual proprietor's full name`
     OR e's `a firm of 2 or more individuals carrying on business under only the full names of all the individuals`
     OR `the profession exemption in section 4(1)(c) applies` e
     OR e's `another person carries on business for the person wholly or mainly as nominee or trustee and has provided the particulars required under section 7(1)`
     OR `the person is within section 4(1)(e) to (o)` e
     OR e's `a person or class of persons for the time being exempted by the Minister under regulations made under section 43`
     OR e's `an individual proprietor who carried on a business specified in the First Schedule to the Business Registration Act immediately before 3 January 2016, is alive and continues to carry on the same business`

-- The exemptions are from a requirement that applies "when carrying on business in
-- Singapore"; the first argument is whether the person does (section 2(2) and (3)).

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, ss 4(1) and 5(1)"
GIVEN `the person carries on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS AN `Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is required to be registered` IF
        `the person carries on business in Singapore`
    AND NOT `the person is not required to be registered under section 4(1)` e

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 4(3)"
GIVEN `the person carries on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS AN `Exemption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may choose to be registered` IF
        `the person carries on business in Singapore`
    AND `the person is not required to be registered under section 4(1)` e
    AND NOT `the person is within section 4(1)(e) to (o)` e

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 4(4)"
GIVEN `the person chose to be registered though not required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is subject to and must comply with the Act` IF
        `the person chose to be registered though not required`
    AND `the person is registered`

-- 4(5): "a reference to an individual or a person includes a class of individuals or a
-- class of persons": a rule of construction, inert.
